{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc 'ls -la; command -v amrfinder abricate rgi resfinder blastn python python3; printenv PATH'", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "total 0\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 applemacbookpro  staff  128 Nov 15 16:18 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 applemacbookpro  staff  160 Nov 15 16:18 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 applemacbookpro  staff  128 Nov 15 16:18 data\ndrwxr-xr-x  6 applemacbookpro  staff  192 Nov 15 16:26 output\n/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/bin/amrfinder\n/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/bin/blastn\n/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/bin/python\n/usr/bin/python3\n/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-darwin-x64/vendor/x86_64-apple-darwin/codex-path:/Users/applemacbookpro/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/applemacbookpro/.codex/tmp/arg0-macos/codex-arg07t9CMH:/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-darwin-x64/vendor/x86_64-apple-darwin/codex-path:/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/bin:/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/bin:/Users/applemacbookpro/.local/bin:/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/condabin\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_2", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_001"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc 'cat data/antibiotics.txt; ls -la output; amrfinder --version; amrfinder --help; blastn -version; python --version'", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "ampicillin\ncefotaxime\nciprofloxacin\ngentamicin\nmeropenem\ntrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 applemacbookpro  staff   192 Nov 15 16:26 .\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 applemacbookpro  staff   128 Nov 15 16:18 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  17 applemacbookpro  staff   544 Nov 15 16:26 amrfinder\n-rw-r--r--   1 applemacbookpro  staff  1686 Nov 15 16:23 assembly_qc.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 applemacbookpro  staff  2577 Nov 15 16:24 make_predictions.py\n-rw-r--r--   1 applemacbookpro  staff  5514 Nov 15 16:26 methods.md\n4.2.7\nIdentify AMR and virulence genes in proteins and/or contigs and print a report\n\nUSAGE:   amrfinder [--update] [--force_update] [--protein PROT_FASTA] [--nucleotide NUC_FASTA] [--gff GFF_FILE] [--annotation_format ANNOTATION_FORMAT] [--database DATABASE_DIR] [--database_version] [--ident_min MIN_IDENT] [--coverage_min MIN_COV] [--organism ORGANISM] [--list_organisms] [--translation_table TRANSLATION_TABLE] [--plus] [--report_common] [--report_all_equal] [--name NAME] [--print_node] [--mutation_all MUT_ALL_FILE] [--output OUTPUT_FILE] [--protein_output PROT_FASTA_OUT] [--nucleotide_output NUC_FASTA_OUT] [--nucleotide_flank5_output NUC_FLANK5_FASTA_OUT] [--nucleotide_flank5_size NUC_FLANK5_SIZE] [--blast_bin BLAST_DIR] [--hmmer_bin HMMER_DIR] [--pgap] [--gpipe_org] [--parm PARM] [--threads THREADS] [--debug] [--log LOG] [--quiet]\nHELP:    amrfinder --help or amrfinder -h\nVERSION: amrfinder --version or amrfinder -v\n\nNAMED PARAMETERS\n-u, --update\n    Update the AMRFinder database\n-U, --force_update\n    Force updating the AMRFinder database\n-p PROT_FASTA, --protein PROT_FASTA\n    Input protein FASTA file (can be gzipped)\n-n NUC_FASTA, --nucleotide NUC_FASTA\n    Input nucleotide FASTA file (can be gzipped)\n-g GFF_FILE, --gff GFF_FILE\n    GFF file for protein locations (can be gzipped). Locations are in the --nucleotide file. Protein ids should be in the attribute 'Name=<id>' (9th field) of the rows with type 'CDS' or 'gene' (3rd field).\n-a ANNOTATION_FORMAT, --annotation_format ANNOTATION_FORMAT\n    Type of GFF file: bakta, genbank, microscope, patric, pgap, prodigal, prokka, pseudomonasdb, rast, standard\n    Default: genbank\n-d DATABASE_DIR, --database DATABASE_DIR\n    Alternative directory with AMRFinder database. Default: $AMRFINDER_DB\n-V, --database_version\n    Print database version and exit\n-i MIN_IDENT, --ident_min MIN_IDENT\n    Minimum proportion of identical amino acids in alignment for hit (0..1). -1 means use a curated threshold if it exists and 0.9 otherwise\n    Default: -1\n-c MIN_COV, --coverage_min MIN_COV\n    Minimum coverage of the reference protein (0..1)\n    Default: 0.5\n-O ORGANISM, --organism ORGANISM\n    Taxonomy group. To see all possible taxonomy groups use the --list_organisms flag\n-l, --list_organisms\n    Print the list of all possible taxonomy groups for mutations identification and exit\n-t TRANSLATION_TABLE, --translation_table TRANSLATION_TABLE\n    NCBI genetic code for translated BLAST\n    Default: 11\n--plus\n    Add the plus genes to the report\n--report_common\n    Report proteins common to a taxonomy group\n--report_all_equal\n    Report all equally-scoring BLAST and HMM matches\n--name NAME\n    Text to be added as the first column \"name\" to all rows of the report, for example it can be an assembly name\n--print_node\n    Print hierarchy node (family)\n--mutation_all MUT_ALL_FILE\n    File to report all mutations\n-o OUTPUT_FILE, --output OUTPUT_FILE\n    Write output to OUTPUT_FILE instead of STDOUT\n--protein_output PROT_FASTA_OUT\n    Output protein FASTA file of reported proteins\n--nucleotide_output NUC_FASTA_OUT\n    Output nucleotide FASTA file of reported nucleotide sequences\n--nucleotide_flank5_output NUC_FLANK5_FASTA_OUT\n    Output nucleotide FASTA file of reported nucleotide sequences with 5' flanking sequences\n--nucleotide_flank5_size NUC_FLANK5_SIZE\n    5' flanking sequence size for NUC_FLANK5_FASTA_OUT\n    Default: 0\n--blast_bin BLAST_DIR\n    Directory for BLAST. Deafult: $BLAST_BIN\n--hmmer_bin HMMER_DIR\n    Directory for HMMer\n--pgap\n    Input files PROT_FASTA, NUC_FASTA and GFF_FILE are created by the NCBI PGAP\n--gpipe_org\n    NCBI internal GPipe organism names\n--parm PARM\n    amr_report parameters for testing: -nosame -noblast -skip_hmm_check -bed\n--threads THREADS\n    Max. number of threads\n    Default: 4\n--debug\n    Integrity checks\n--log LOG\n    Error log file, appended, opened on application start\n-q, --quiet\n    Suppress messages to STDERR\n\nTemporary directory used is $TMPDIR or \"/tmp\"\n\nDOCUMENTATION\n    See https://github.com/ncbi/amr/wiki for full documentation\n\nUPDATES\n    Subscribe to the amrfinder-announce mailing list for database and software update notifications: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mailman/listinfo/amrfinder-announce\nblastn: 2.17.0+\n Package: blast 2.17.0, build Aug 22 2026 13:45:01\nPython 3.13.13\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_3", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_001"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc 'cat output/methods.md; cat output/make_predictions.py; ls -l output/amrfinder; cat output/assembly_qc.json; amrfinder --database_version'", "exit_code": 1, "stdout": "# Genome-only resistance predictions\n\nInputs were all ten `data/genomes/ISO_*.fasta` assemblies, treated as Escherichia coli as specified, and the six exact antibiotic names in `data/antibiotics.txt`. No phenotype, isolate metadata, internet access, downloads, or external services were used. `assembly_qc.json` records sequence lengths, contig counts, ambiguous-base counts and SHA-256 input checksums, calculated with Python standard-library code. Assemblies were not modified.\n\n## Software and local database\n\n- NCBI AMRFinderPlus **4.2.7**, checked with `amrfinder --version`.\n- NCBI BLAST+ **2.17.0+**, build August 22, 2026; `blastn`, `blastp`, `blastx`, and `tblastn` versions checked before their analyses. Nucleotide-only AMRFinder logs show that the actual searches used `tblastn` and `blastn`.\n- HMMER **3.4** (August 2023), checked using `hmmsearch -h`; available but no protein/HMM search was requested in this nucleotide-only workflow.\n- Python **3.9.6**, checked using `python3 --version`; standard library only for orchestration, assembly summaries, parsing and prediction generation.\n- NCBI AMRFinderPlus database **2026-10-29.1**, explicitly verified using `amrfinder -d DB --database_version`, where DB was `/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1`. The default database path did not resolve, so the installed database was supplied explicitly. No database was updated. The database's protein reference catalogue, hierarchy/curated cutoffs, Escherichia protein mutation catalogue and Escherichia DNA mutation references were used through AMRFinder.\n\nExecutable discovery found AMRFinderPlus and BLAST+ on PATH; ABRicate, RGI and ResFinder executables were not on PATH. All resistance searches used the single local database above.\n\n## Search parameters and reproducibility\n\nFor each isolate, the command was:\n\n```\namrfinder -d /Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1 \\\n  -n data/genomes/ISO_XXX.fasta -O Escherichia --threads 2 \\\n  --mutation_all output/amrfinder/ISO_XXX.mutations.tsv \\\n  -o output/amrfinder/ISO_XXX.tsv\n```\n\nStandard output/error were retained in `output/amrfinder/ISO_XXX.log`. Up to three independent isolates were run concurrently. No `--plus`, `--report_common`, protein annotation, or custom identity/coverage search options were supplied. AMRFinder defaults were used: curated identity threshold when present, otherwise 0.9; minimum reference coverage 0.5; genetic code 11. The organism option enables curated Escherichia resistance mutation detection. The mutation-all tables retain wild-type and unknown changes for audit; only resistance mutations in the primary report can drive R calls.\n\n`output/make_predictions.py` implements the genotype-to-phenotype rules and can be rerun from the workspace. Only primary-report AMR entries with at least 90% reference coverage and 90% identity, excluding PARTIAL methods, are eligible to drive calls. This additional filter avoids treating short fragments as functional determinants. Allele labels and amino acid changes are reported as assigned by AMRFinder. Unknown substitutions and ordinary intrinsic genes are not inferred to confer resistance.\n\n## Translation to calls\n\nThese are qualitative genome-based predictions, without MIC estimation or a specified clinical breakpoint system:\n\n- **Ampicillin:** R for an eligible acquired `bla` beta-lactamase, including TEM, OXA, CTX-M, acquired AmpC and carbapenemases.\n- **Cefotaxime:** R for CTX-M or another explicitly annotated extended-spectrum beta-lactamase, acquired AmpC families CMY/DHA/FOX/ACT/MIR/ACC/MOX/LAT, or KPC/NDM/VIM/IMP. Narrow-spectrum TEM-1 and OXA-1 alone do not drive this call.\n- **Meropenem:** R for KPC/NDM/VIM/IMP, OXA-48-like alleles (OXA-48/181/232/244), or a reference explicitly annotated as a carbapenem resistance enzyme. ESBL alone does not drive meropenem resistance.\n- **Gentamicin:** R only for an eligible entry whose curated Subclass includes GENTAMICIN. Streptomycin-only aadA and amikacin/kanamycin/tobramycin AAC(6')-Ib entries do not drive this call.\n- **Ciprofloxacin:** curated gyrA resistance substitutions drive R; accompanying gyrB/parC mutations, qnr, qepA, oqx and AAC(6')-Ib-cr determinants are included in evidence where present. A low-level plasmid mechanism or isolated parC/gyrB determinant without a gyrA change is assigned NA because clinical resistance is uncertain. ParE I529L alone is not used to predict resistance.\n- **Trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole:** R if an eligible acquired dfr or sul determinant is present, using a conservative resistance rule for either component; all detected eligible dfr and sul genes are listed. A single component's determinant is less certain than determinants for both components.\n- **S:** no eligible determinant relevant to that antibiotic was found. Evidence is exactly `no determinant found`. S is an absence-based prediction, not proof of phenotypic susceptibility.\n\nRegulatory changes, expression, heteroresistance, novel alleles, porin defects, ESBL/AmpC plus permeability effects and unrepresented mechanisms may cause discordance. Chromosomal ampC promoter variation and non-curated regulatory/porin variants were not independently analyzed. Fragmented or incomplete assemblies can conceal determinants; the 90% coverage filter can miss disrupted or split genes. These limitations particularly affect absence-based S calls. No clinical susceptibility measurements or outcome claims are made.\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\nantibiotics=Path('data/antibiotics.txt').read_text().splitlines()\nallrows=[]\nfor assembly in sorted(Path('data/genomes').glob('*.fasta')):\n    isolate=assembly.stem\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(open(f'output/amrfinder/{isolate}.tsv'),delimiter='\\t'))\n    hits=[r for r in rows if r['Type']=='AMR' and float(r['% Coverage of reference'])>=90 and float(r['% Identity to reference'])>=90 and not r['Method'].startswith('PARTIAL')]\n    genes={r['Element symbol']:r for r in hits}\n    for drug in antibiotics:\n        determinants=[]\n        for g,r in genes.items():\n            name=r['Element name'].lower(); sub=r['Subclass'].split('/')\n            if drug=='ampicillin' and g.startswith('bla'): determinants.append(g)\n            elif drug=='cefotaxime' and (g.startswith(('blaCTX-M','blaCMY','blaDHA','blaFOX','blaACT','blaMIR','blaACC','blaMOX','blaLAT','blaKPC','blaNDM','blaVIM','blaIMP')) or ('extended-spectrum' in name and g.startswith('bla'))): determinants.append(g)\n            elif drug=='meropenem' and (g.startswith(('blaKPC','blaNDM','blaVIM','blaIMP','blaOXA-48','blaOXA-181','blaOXA-232','blaOXA-244')) or 'carbapenem' in name): determinants.append(g)\n            elif drug=='gentamicin' and 'GENTAMICIN' in sub: determinants.append(g)\n            elif drug=='ciprofloxacin' and (g.startswith(('gyrA_','gyrB_','parC_')) or g.startswith(('qnr','qepA','oqx')) or (g.startswith('aac(6\\')-Ib-cr'))): determinants.append(g)\n            elif drug=='trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole' and (g.startswith(('dfr','sul'))): determinants.append(g)\n        # A single parC change or only a low-level plasmid quinolone determinant\n        # is insufficient to infer clinical ciprofloxacin resistance reliably.\n        if drug=='ciprofloxacin' and determinants and not any(g.startswith('gyrA_') for g in determinants):\n            prediction='NA'; evidence='; '.join(sorted(determinants))+'; low-level/isolated determinant, clinical category uncertain'\n        else:\n            prediction='R' if determinants else 'S'\n            evidence='; '.join(sorted(determinants)) if determinants else 'no determinant found'\n        allrows.append([isolate,drug,prediction,evidence])\nwith open('output/predictions.tsv','w',newline='') as f:\n    w=csv.writer(f,delimiter='\\t'); w.writerow(['isolate_id','antibiotic','prediction','evidence']); w.writerows(allrows)\nassert len(allrows)==len(list(Path('data/genomes').glob('*.fasta')))*len(antibiotics)\nassert len({(r[0],r[1]) for r in allrows})==len(allrows)\nprint(f'Validated {len(allrows)} predictions')\ntotal 648\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    605 Nov 15 16:22 ISO_001.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff  69075 Nov 15 16:22 ISO_001.mutations.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff   4844 Nov 15 16:22 ISO_001.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    538 Nov 15 16:22 ISO_002.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    538 Nov 15 16:22 ISO_003.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    605 Nov 15 16:24 ISO_004.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff  71996 Nov 15 16:24 ISO_004.mutations.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff   1437 Nov 15 16:24 ISO_004.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    605 Nov 15 16:25 ISO_005.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff  62681 Nov 15 16:25 ISO_005.mutations.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff   5691 Nov 15 16:25 ISO_005.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    605 Nov 15 16:26 ISO_006.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff  62184 Nov 15 16:26 ISO_006.mutations.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff   5550 Nov 15 16:26 ISO_006.tsv\n-rw-r--r--  1 applemacbookpro  staff    538 Nov 15 16:26 ISO_007.log\n{\n  \"ISO_001\": {\n    \"contigs\": 196,\n    \"bases\": 5331204,\n    \"ambiguous_bases\": 0,\n    \"sha256\": \"9c8f93ca0469a0c2c5d3357db511b60f56132ca6016759df6b0394d960ab2e18\"\n  },\n  \"ISO_002\": {\n    \"contigs\": 4,\n    \"bases\": 5085165,\n    \"ambiguous_bases\": 0,\n    \"sha256\": \"7c90e7a1038b1ddbe393aa44c4aae3829efe696731ab22a383e91604f5adbdc0\"\n  },\n  \"ISO_003\": {\n    \"contigs\": 7,\n    \"bases\": 5235096,\n    \"ambiguous_bases\": 300,\n    \"sha256\": \"053576be40bd03a90bb230ce0aaffadb3a0879a8f32a39e419