{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('output/chunked_genomes'); p.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor f in Path('data/genomes').glob('*.fasta'):\n if Path('output/amrfinder',f.stem+'.tsv').exists(): continue\n records=[]; name=None; seq=[]\n for line in f.read_text().splitlines():\n  if line.startswith('>'):\n   if name: records.append((name,''.join(seq)))\n   name=line[1:].split()[0]; seq=[]\n  else: seq.append(line.strip())\n if name: records.append((name,''.join(seq)))\n with (p/f.name).open('w') as out:\n  for name,s in records:\n   for start in range(0,len(s),27000): out.write('>'+name+'__offset_'+str(start)+'\\\\n'+s[start:start+30000]+'\\\\n')\nprint('prepared overlapping chunks')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "prepared overlapping chunks\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_15", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_001"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('output/make_predictions.py'); s=p.read_text(); s=s.replace(\\\"rows=list(csv.DictReader(open(f'output/amrfinder/{isolate}.tsv'),delimiter='\\\\\\\\t'))\\\", \\\"report=Path(f'output/amrfinder_chunked/{isolate}.tsv')\\\\n    if not report.exists(): report=Path(f'output/amrfinder/{isolate}.tsv')\\\\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(report.open(),delimiter='\\\\\\\\t'))\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('output/methods.md'); s=p.read_text(); s=s.replace('Assemblies were not modified.','Original assemblies were preserved. For isolates lacking a completed original-assembly report, derived overlapping windows were searched as described below.')\ns=s.replace('\"'`output/make_predictions.py` implements'\"', '''## Long-contig search adjustment\n\nOriginal-assembly runs for ISO_002, ISO_003 and ISO_007 were unusually slow in translated searches. For ISO_002, ISO_003, ISO_007, ISO_008, ISO_009 and ISO_010, each original contig was divided into windows of at most 30,000 nt at a stride of 27,000 nt (3,000 nt overlap), without changing bases. Window headers append \"'`__offset_START`, with zero-based original-contig offsets. Derived FASTA files are retained in `output/chunked_genomes/`. The identical AMRFinder command and database were used with `-n output/chunked_genomes/ISO_XXX.fasta`, and reports/logs were written under `output/amrfinder_chunked/`. Up to three windowed searches ran concurrently. These windowed reports take precedence in prediction generation; repeated hits in overlaps are collapsed by element symbol. The overlap exceeds the length of the main acquired resistance genes and quinolone targets used for these predictions. Positions in windowed reports are relative to the window. Earlier unwindowed runs and any incomplete logs are not used when a windowed report exists.\n\n`output/make_predictions.py` implements'\"''')\np.write_text(s)\nprint('Updated reproducible calling script and methods for windowed searches')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "Updated reproducible calling script and methods for windowed searches\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_18", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_001"}
