{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > output/methods.md <<'EOF'\n# Genome-based resistance predictions\n\nAll ten supplied Escherichia coli assemblies were searched locally, without internet access, against the installed NCBI AMRFinderPlus database. No phenotype data or isolate metadata were used.\n\n## Software and database\n\n- AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7 (queried with \"'`amrfinder --version`).\n- NCBI AMRFinderPlus database 2026-10-29.1 (confirmed with `amrfinder -d <database> --database_version`). Explicit database directory: `/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1`. The default database path did not exist; the installed database was supplied explicitly. No update was attempted.\n- NCBI BLAST+ 2.17.0+ (build Aug 22 2026); `blastn`, `blastx`, `tblastn`, and `blastp` versions were inspected. The nucleotide-only AMRFinder workflow uses translated nucleotide searches and nucleotide mutation searches; no independent BLAST analysis was added.\n- HMMER 3.4 (Aug 2023), inspected with `hmmsearch -h`; no independent HMM search was performed.\n- Python 3.9.6 standard library for job orchestration, TSV parsing, rule application, and output validation.\n\nAMRFinderPlus and BLAST were available on PATH; ABRicate, RGI, ResFinder and PointFinder executables were not found on PATH. `--list_organisms` confirmed that `Escherichia` is supported.\n\n## Search procedure\n\nFor every `data/genomes/ISO_###.fasta`:\n\n```sh\namrfinder -n data/genomes/ISO_###.fasta '\"\\\\\n  -d /Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1 \\\\\n  -O Escherichia --threads 2 \\\\\n  --mutation_all output/amrfinder/ISO_###.mutations.tsv \\\\\n  -o output/amrfinder/ISO_###.tsv\n\"'```\n\nISO_011 used four threads; other isolates used two threads, with at most two isolate searches running concurrently. Other options were defaults: curated identity thresholds where available, otherwise 90% identity; minimum reference coverage 50%; translation table 11; core report, without `--plus` or `--report_common`. No protein annotation was supplied. AMRFinder searches its bundled resistance protein/reference hierarchy and Escherichia protein/DNA mutation catalogs. Raw resistance reports and all-site mutation reports are retained in `output/amrfinder/`. Wild-type/unknown variants in the all-site reports are not treated as resistance determinants.\n\n## Genotype-to-prediction rules\n\nThe accompanying `output/call_predictions.py` implements the exact rules and records the determinants driving each positive call. Calls use the main AMRFinder report, with an additional minimum 90% reference coverage for acquired genes, excluding interrupted/internal-stop matches. Curated resistance point mutations are retained. These are deterministic genomic predictions, not measured MICs or breakpoint-based susceptibility tests.\n\n- Ampicillin: acquired beta-lactamases, including narrow-spectrum TEM/OXA enzymes, ESBLs, acquired AmpC enzymes, and carbapenemases predict R. Native basal chromosomal ampC is not by itself counted.\n- Cefotaxime: CTX-M ESBLs, identified ESBL TEM/SHV variants, acquired AmpC enzymes, and broad-spectrum carbapenemases (NDM/KPC/VIM/IMP) predict R. TEM-1, OXA-10 and OXA-48 alone do not predict cefotaxime resistance. Recognized ampC regulatory resistance variants also count.\n- Meropenem: an acquired carbapenemase predicts R, including OXA-48 even though its MIC effect varies. Porin or target mutations alone do not establish meropenem resistance.\n- Ciprofloxacin: recognized GyrA/ParC resistance substitutions or acquired quinolone/fluoroquinolone determinants (qnr, qepA, oqxAB, aac(6'\"')-Ib-cr) predict R. Low-level determinants can yield MICs below clinical resistance breakpoints; this rule favors detecting genomic resistance potential. Isolated ParE or general efflux-regulator variants are not sufficient.\n- Gentamicin: acquired determinants with GENTAMICIN in the curated subclass, or broad aminoglycoside resistance 16S methylases (armA/rmt/npmA), predict R. Streptomycin/kanamycin-specific aadA/aph genes do not count.\n- Trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole: a trimethoprim-resistant dfr determinant predicts R; accompanying sul genes are also reported. Sul alone is insufficient to establish resistance to the combination.\n\nS means no qualifying resistance determinant was found for that antibiotic under these rules; evidence is \"'`no determinant found`. It does not prove phenotypic susceptibility. Expression, novel determinants, promoter variation beyond the curated catalog, copy number, permeability, assembly gaps, and interactions between mechanisms may affect real susceptibility. NA is reserved for a failed/uninterpretable genome search. No external reference download or clinical breakpoint table was used.\nEOF'", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_13", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_002"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > output/call_predictions.py <<'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nantibiotics = (ROOT / 'data/antibiotics.txt').read_text().splitlines()\n\ndef determinants(rows, drug):\n    valid = []\n    for r in rows:\n        g, sub = r['Element symbol'], r['Subclass']\n        point = r['Subtype'] == 'POINT'\n        if not point and (float(r['% Coverage of reference']) < 90 or 'INTERNAL_STOP' in r['Method'] or 'INTERNAL_STOP' in r['Element name']):\n            continue\n        low = g.lower()\n        beta = g.startswith('bla')\n        carb = beta and (sub == 'CARBAPENEM' or low.startswith(('blandm','blakpc','blavim','blaimp','blaoxa-48','blaoxa-181','blaoxa-232')))\n        esbl = beta and (low.startswith(('blactx-m','blacmy','bladha','blafox','blaacc','blaact','blamir','blamox','blandm','blakpc','blavim','blaimp')) or ('extended-spectrum' in r['Element name'].lower()))\n        yes = False\n        if drug == 'ampicillin':\n            yes = beta or (point and g.startswith('ampC') and ('AMPICILLIN' in sub or 'CEPHALOSPORIN' in sub))\n        elif drug == 'cefotaxime':\n            yes = esbl or (point and g.startswith('ampC') and ('CEPHALOSPORIN' in sub))\n        elif drug == 'meropenem':\n            yes = carb\n        elif drug == 'ciprofloxacin':\n            yes = (point and g.startswith(('gyrA_', 'parC_'))) or (not point and (low.startswith(('qnr','qepa','oqxa','oqxb')) or (low.startswith('aac(6\\\\')-ib') and '-cr' in low)))\n        elif drug == 'gentamicin':\n            yes = not point and ('GENTAMICIN' in sub or low.startswith(('arma','rmt','npma')))\n        elif drug == 'trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole':\n            yes = (g.startswith('dfr') and 'TRIMETHOPRIM' in sub)\n        if yes:\n            valid.append(g)\n    if drug == 'trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole' and valid:\n        valid.extend(r['Element symbol'] for r in rows if r['Element symbol'].startswith('sul') and float(r['% Coverage of reference']) >= 90)\n    return sorted(set(valid))\n\nout = []\nfor genome in sorted((ROOT / 'data/genomes').glob('*.fasta')):\n    report = ROOT / 'output/amrfinder' / (genome.stem + '.tsv')\n    assert report.exists(), report\n    with report.open() as f:\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(f, delimiter='\\\\t'))\n    for drug in antibiotics:\n        evidence = determinants(rows, drug)\n        out.append([genome.stem, drug, 'R' if evidence else 'S', '; '.join(evidence) if evidence else 'no determinant found'])\nassert len(out) == len(list((ROOT / 'data/genomes').glob('*.fasta'))) * len(antibiotics)\nassert len({(r[0], r[1]) for r in out}) == len(out)\nwith (ROOT / 'output/predictions.tsv').open('w') as f:\n    w = csv.writer(f, delimiter='\\\\t', lineterminator='\\\\n')\n    w.writerow(['isolate_id', 'antibiotic', 'prediction', 'evidence'])\n    w.writerows(out)\nprint(f'Wrote and validated {len(out)} isolate-antibiotic predictions')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_15", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_002"}
