{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('output/call_predictions.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"if not point and (float(r['% Coverage of reference']) < 90 or\\\", \\\"end_partial = r['Method'] == 'PARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX' and float(r['% Coverage of reference']) >= 80 and float(r['% Identity to reference']) >= 99\\\\n        if not point and ((float(r['% Coverage of reference']) < 90 and not end_partial) or\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('output/methods.md');s=p.read_text().replace('with an additional minimum 90% reference coverage for acquired genes, excluding interrupted/internal-stop matches.', 'with an additional minimum 90% reference coverage for acquired genes, excluding interrupted/internal-stop matches. Contig-end partial matches are accepted at >=80% reference coverage and >=99% identity because missing sequence can reflect assembly fragmentation. This exception accepts ISO_017 aac(3)-IId (86.71% coverage, 100% identity, PARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX) for gentamicin resistance; the assembly does not establish whether the missing end is intact.')\ns += '\\\\n## Output validation\\\\n\\\\nAll ten searches completed successfully. The final TSV contains exactly 60 unique isolate–antibiotic pairs, the requested four columns, and only S/R calls with nonempty evidence. Calls comprise 24 R and 36 S; no NA calls were required.\\\\n'\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 output/call_predictions.py\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "Wrote and validated 60 isolate-antibiotic predictions\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_25", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_002"}
