{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc 'cat output/amrfinder/ISO_036.log; shasum -a 256 data/antibiotics.txt data/genomes/*.fasta > output/input_sha256.txt'", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "Running: amrfinder -n data/genomes/ISO_036.fasta -O Escherichia -d /Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1 --threads 4 --mutation_all output/amrfinder/ISO_036.mutations.tsv -o output/amrfinder/ISO_036.tsv\nSoftware directory: /Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/bin/\nSoftware version: 4.2.7\nDatabase directory: /Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1\nDatabase version: 2026-10-29.1\nAMRFinder translated nucleotide and mutation search\nRunning tblastn\nperl: warning: Setting locale failed.\nperl: warning: Please check that your locale settings:\n\tLC_ALL = \"C.UTF-8\",\n\tLC_CTYPE = \"C.UTF-8\",\n\tLANG = \"tr_TR.UTF-8\"\n    are supported and installed on your system.\nperl: warning: Falling back to a fallback locale (\"tr_TR.UTF-8\").\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_25", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_004"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('output/methods.md').write_text('''# Genome-based antimicrobial susceptibility predictions\n\n## Inputs and scope\nAll 10 supplied E. coli assemblies (ISO_031 through ISO_040) were screened against a locally installed resistance database. Antibiotic names and order were read directly from \"'`data/antibiotics.txt`. No internet access, database update, download, phenotype labels, or external isolate metadata were used. Input SHA-256 checksums are retained in `input_sha256.txt`. Basic FASTA counts are retained in `assembly_qc.json`; assemblies are 4.68–5.28 Mb, with 81–261 contigs and 0–92 ambiguous N bases. These checks do not establish completeness or exclude contamination.\n\n## Software and database\nVersions were checked before analysis using `amrfinder --version`, BLAST executables'\"' \"'`-version`, `hmmsearch -h`, and `python3 --version`.\n\n- NCBI AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7, executable `/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/bin/amrfinder`.\n- NCBI AMRFinderPlus database **2026-10-29.1**, database format **4.2.0**, at `/Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1`. Confirmed with `amrfinder -d <database> --database_version`. Organism support was verified using `--list_organisms`.\n- NCBI BLAST+ 2.17.0+ (blastn, blastp, blastx, tblastn version checks; AMRFinder'\"'s nucleotide workflow actually ran tblastn and blastn).\n- HMMER 3.4 (Aug 2023), available and version checked; no separate HMMER search was run because inputs were nucleotide assemblies, without protein annotations.\n- Python 3.9.6 standard library for FASTA checks, report parsing, prediction generation, and output validation.\n\nThe default AMRFinder database path was invalid. The installed database was located locally and explicitly supplied; the initial default-path version query failed before any genome analysis. ABRicate, RGI, ResFinder, PointFinder, minimap2, and samtools were not on PATH. No installation was attempted.\n\n## Search parameters and retained evidence\nFor each isolate, the exact command template was:\n\n\"'```sh\namrfinder -n data/genomes/ISO_XXX.fasta '\"\\\\\\\\\n  -O Escherichia \\\\\\\\\n  -d /Users/applemacbookpro/miniforge3/envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1 \\\\\\\\\n  --threads 4 \\\\\\\\\n  --mutation_all output/amrfinder/ISO_XXX.mutations.tsv \\\\\\\\\n  -o output/amrfinder/ISO_XXX.tsv \\\\\\\\\n  > output/amrfinder/ISO_XXX.log 2>&1\n\"'```\n\nSearch used default identity threshold `--ident_min -1` (curated threshold where available, otherwise 90%), minimum reference coverage `--coverage_min 0.5`, and translation table 11. Neither `--plus` nor `--report_common` was enabled. No annotations or gene-calling tool were required. Escherichia-specific protein and nucleotide mutation searches were enabled. The main report contains recognized resistance determinants; mutation_all additionally records wild-type and unknown states, which were not treated as resistance determinants. Coordinates, coverage, identity, reference accessions, and detection methods remain in the raw TSVs. No extra BLAST searches or custom reference databases were used.\n\n## Translation to calls\nCalls are deterministic genome-based estimates, not measured MICs or validated clinical susceptibility tests. No explicit EUCAST/CLSI breakpoint version or trained classifier was applied. `S` means the completed screen found no determinant judged sufficient for resistance to that particular drug. Absence of a database hit cannot exclude novel mechanisms, expression changes, porin defects, or assembly gaps. `NA` is used when detected evidence is insufficient to resolve a call.\n\nDrug rules and the exact observed determinants are recorded below after completion of all screens. Database drug classes were interpreted by substrate specificity rather than transferring resistance to every member of a class. Intrinsic wild-type chromosomal functions and unrelated resistance determinants were not counted. The reproducible decision logic is retained in `make_predictions.py`.\n'\"''')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_27", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_004"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv,pathlib\nfor p in sorted(pathlib.Path('output/amrfinder').glob('ISO_???.tsv')):\n rows=list(csv.DictReader(p.open(),delimiter='\\\\t'))\n print(p.stem, '; '.join(r['Element symbol']+' ['+r['Subclass']+']' for r in rows if r['Class'] in ('BETA-LACTAM','AMINOGLYCOSIDE','QUINOLONE','TRIMETHOPRIM','SULFONAMIDE','MULTIDRUG')))\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "ISO_031 parC_E84V [QUINOLONE]; parC_S80I [QUINOLONE]; parE_I529L [QUINOLONE]; sul1 [SULFONAMIDE]; aadA5 [STREPTOMYCIN]; dfrA17 [TRIMETHOPRIM]; blaTEM-1 [BETA-LACTAM]; gyrA_D87N [QUINOLONE]; gyrA_S83L [QUINOLONE]\nISO_032 aph(6)-Id [STREPTOMYCIN]; aph(3'')-Ib [STREPTOMYCIN]\nISO_033 marR_S3N [AMPICILLIN/CHLORAMPHENICOL/QUINOLONE/RIFAMPIN/TETRACYCLINE]\nISO_034 \nISO_035 blaTEM-1 [BETA-LACTAM]; sul2 [SULFONAMIDE]; aph(3')-Ia [KANAMYCIN]; dfrA17 [TRIMETHOPRIM]; aadA5 [STREPTOMYCIN]; sul1 [SULFONAMIDE]; sul3 [SULFONAMIDE]; aadA1 [STREPTOMYCIN]; aadA2 [STREPTOMYCIN]; aph(6)-Id [STREPTOMYCIN]; aph(3'')-Ib [STREPTOMYCIN]; aac(3)-IId [GENTAMICIN]; gyrA_S83L [QUINOLONE]; cirA_S38LfsTer29 [CEFIDEROCOL]\nISO_036 marR_S3N [AMPICILLIN/CHLORAMPHENICOL/QUINOLONE/RIFAMPIN/TETRACYCLINE]\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_28", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_004"}
{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > output/make_predictions.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Generate drug-specific calls from retained AMRFinderPlus reports; run from workspace.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nOUT = ROOT / 'output'\nantibiotics = (ROOT / 'data/antibiotics.txt').read_text().splitlines()\nassert antibiotics == ['ampicillin', 'cefotaxime', 'ciprofloxacin', 'gentamicin', 'meropenem', 'trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole']\nresults = []\nfor fasta in sorted((ROOT / 'data/genomes').glob('ISO_*.fasta')):\n    isolate = fasta.stem\n    assert 'seconds to complete' in (OUT / 'amrfinder' / (isolate + '.log')).read_text()\n    with (OUT / 'amrfinder' / (isolate + '.tsv')).open() as handle:\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(handle, delimiter='\\\\t'))\n    symbols = {r['Element symbol'] for r in rows}\n    # These rules are restricted to the observed symbols, with explicit assertions\n    # to prevent silently assigning an unseen beta-lactamase a substrate spectrum.\n    beta = {r['Element symbol'] for r in rows if r['Class'] == 'BETA-LACTAM' and r['Subtype'] == 'AMR'}\n    assert all(g.startswith(('blaTEM-', 'blaCTX-M-', 'blaOXA-', 'blaCMY-', 'blaNDM-', 'blaKPC-', 'blaSHV-')) for g in beta), beta\n    esbl = {r['Element symbol'] for r in rows if r['Element symbol'].startswith(('blaCTX-M-', 'blaCMY-')) or 'extended-spectrum' in r['Element name'].lower()}\n    carb = {r['Element symbol'] for r in rows if 'carbapenem' in r['Element name'].lower() or r['Element symbol'].startswith(('blaNDM-', 'blaKPC-', 'blaVIM-', 'blaIMP-', 'blaOXA-48', 'blaOXA-181', 'blaOXA-232'))}\n    gent = {r['Element symbol'] for r in rows if 'GENTAMICIN' in r['Subclass'].split('/')}\n    dfr = {g for g in symbols if g.startswith('dfr')}\n    sul = {g for g in symbols if g.startswith('sul')}\n    qrdr = {g for g in symbols if g.startswith(('gyrA_S83', 'gyrA_D87', 'gyrB_', 'parC_S80', 'parC_E84'))}\n    pmqr = {g for g in symbols if g.startswith(('qnr', 'qepA', 'oqx')) or g == 'aac(6\\\\')-Ib-cr'}\n    for antibiotic in antibiotics:\n        prediction, evidence = 'S', 'no determinant found'\n        genes = set()\n        if antibiotic == 'ampicillin':\n            genes = beta\n            if not genes and 'marR_S3N' in symbols:\n                prediction, evidence = 'NA', 'marR_S3N only; regulatory effect insufficient to resolve phenotype'\n        elif antibiotic == 'cefotaxime':\n            genes = esbl | carb\n        elif antibiotic == 'meropenem':\n            genes = carb\n        elif antibiotic == 'gentamicin':\n            genes = gent\n        elif antibiotic == 'ciprofloxacin':\n            genes = qrdr\n            if not genes and (pmqr or 'marR_S3N' in symbols):\n                prediction = 'NA'\n                evidence = '; '.join(sorted(pmqr | (symbols & {'marR_S3N'}))) + ' only; insufficient to resolve phenotype'\n        elif antibiotic == 'trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole':\n            if dfr and sul:\n                genes = dfr | sul\n            elif dfr or sul:\n                prediction, evidence = 'NA', '; '.join(sorted(dfr | sul)) + '; only one component has a determinant'\n        if genes:\n            prediction, evidence = 'R', '; '.join(sorted(genes))\n        results.append(dict(isolate_id=isolate, antibiotic=antibiotic, prediction=prediction, evidence=evidence))\n\nwith (OUT / 'predictions.tsv').open('w', newline='') as handle:\n    writer = csv.DictWriter(handle, fieldnames=['isolate_id','antibiotic','prediction','evidence'], delimiter='\\\\t', lineterminator='\\\\n')\n    writer.writeheader()\n    writer.writerows(results)\nassert len(results) == len(list((ROOT / 'data/genomes').glob('ISO_*.fasta'))) * len(antibiotics)\nassert len({(r['isolate_id'], r['antibiotic']) for r in results}) == len(results)\nassert all(r['prediction'] in {'S','R','NA'} and r['evidence'] for r in results)\nprint('Validated', len(results), 'predictions')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_29", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_004"}
