{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import Counter\np=Path('output/methods.md')\ns=p.read_text().replace('including observed TEM-1 and KPC-3','including observed TEM-1, SHV-1, and KPC-3').replace('TEM-1 alone does not qualify.', 'TEM-1 or SHV-1 alone does not qualify.')\nwith Path('output/predictions.tsv').open() as f:\n reader=csv.DictReader(f,delimiter='\\\\t')\n assert reader.fieldnames==['isolate_id','antibiotic','prediction','evidence']\n rows=list(reader)\nexpected={(p.stem,a) for p in Path('data/genomes').glob('*.fasta') for a in Path('data/antibiotics.txt').read_text().splitlines()}\nassert {(r['isolate_id'],r['antibiotic']) for r in rows}==expected\nassert len(rows)==len(expected)==60\ncounts=Counter(r['prediction'] for r in rows)\ns+='\\\\n## Completed analysis and validation\\\\n\\\\nAll ten AMRFinder runs completed successfully. \"'`predictions.tsv` has exactly the required four columns and 60 unique isolate–antibiotic pairs, covering ten isolates and six antibiotics. Counts: '\"'+', '.join(f'{k}={counts[k]}' for k in ['S','R','NA'])+'. Seven NA calls comprise ampicillin/ciprofloxacin in ISO_033 and ISO_036 (MarR S3N only), and trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole in ISO_037 (dfrA14 only), ISO_038 (sul2 only), and ISO_040 (sul1 only).\\\\n\\\\nObserved acquired beta-lactamases were TEM-1, SHV-1, and KPC-3; all had 100% reference coverage and identity. No qualifying cefotaxime or meropenem determinant other than KPC-3 was detected. Raw reports and successful-run logs are retained under \"'`amrfinder/`. All reported hits exceeded 90% reference coverage and 90% identity; no fragmentary acquired gene was used to drive a resistance call.'\"\\\\n'\np.write_text(s)\nprint(dict(counts))\nfor id in sorted({r['isolate_id'] for r in rows}):\n with Path('output/amrfinder',id+'.mutations.tsv').open() as f:\n  mut=list(csv.DictReader(f,delimiter='\\\\t'))\n target={r['Element symbol'].split('_')[0] for r in mut if 