{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import Counter\nant=Path('data/antibiotics.txt').read_text().splitlines()\nids=[p.stem for p in sorted(Path('data/genomes').glob('*.fasta'))]\np=Path('output/predictions.tsv')\nwith p.open() as f:\n reader=csv.DictReader(f,delimiter='\\\\t'); assert reader.fieldnames==['isolate_id','antibiotic','prediction','evidence']; rows=list(reader)\nassert len(rows)==60\nassert Counter((r['isolate_id'],r['antibiotic']) for r in rows)==Counter((i,a) for i in ids for a in ant)\nassert all(r['prediction'] in {'S','R','NA'} and r['evidence'] and len(r)==4 for r in rows)\nfor i in ids:\n hits=list(csv.DictReader(open('output/'+i+'.amrfinder.tsv'),delimiter='\\\\t'))\n muts=list(csv.DictReader(open('output/'+i+'.mutations.tsv'),delimiter='\\\\t'))\n assert any(r['Element symbol'].startswith('gyrA_') for r in muts),i\n assert any(r['Element symbol'].startswith('parC_') for r in muts),i\n print(i,dict(Counter(r['prediction'] for r in rows if r['isolate_id']==i)))\nprint('PASS: 60 unique complete pairs; correct header, fields, allowed calls; gyrA/parC assessed in every isolate.')\nwith open('output/methods.md','a') as f:\n f.write('\\\\n## Run checks and specific interpretation notes\\\\n\\\\nAll ten searches completed successfully. Input FASTA symbols were validated and SHA-256 checksums, contig counts, and total sequence lengths recorded in \"'`output/input_checksums.tsv`. The final TSV was checked for the exact header, 60 unique isolate–antibiotic pairs, complete Cartesian-product coverage, valid predictions, and nonempty evidence. All isolates had gyrA and parC entries in the all-mutation reports.'\"\\\\n\\\\nDrug-driving acquired genes were full-length matches (100% reference coverage); gyrA mutation alignments covered 99.66% of their reference. Some unrelated resistance genes had partial matches; they did not drive any of the six drug calls. ISO_063 has CMY-2 and ompC_W124Ter: its meropenem S call follows the rule above and carries uncertainty about permeability effects. ISO_069 has a single gyrA_S83L mutation: its ciprofloxacin R call follows the conservative genetic-resistance rule and has greater breakpoint uncertainty than multi-mutation calls. ISO_070 has dfrA1 without a reported sul gene: its combination-drug R call follows the one-component resistance rule. ISO_065 blaTEMp_C32T is supporting promoter evidence alongside intact TEM-1; it is not used to infer cefotaxime resistance.\\\\n')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "ISO_061 {'R': 3, 'S': 3}\nISO_062 {'R': 2, 'S': 4}\nISO_063 {'R': 3, 'S': 3}\nISO_064 {'S': 6}\nISO_065 {'R': 4, 'S': 2}\nISO_066 {'R': 5, 'S': 1}\nISO_067 {'R': 3, 'S': 3}\nISO_068 {'S': 6}\nISO_069 {'R': 4, 'S': 2}\nISO_070 {'R': 4, 'S': 2}\nPASS: 60 unique complete pairs; correct header, fields, allowed calls; gyrA/parC assessed in every isolate.\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_44", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_007"}
