{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('output/make_predictions.py')\ns=p.read_text().replace(\\\"        detail = '; '.join(determinants) if determinants else 'no determinant found'\\\", \\\"        call = 'R' if determinants else 'S'\\\\n        detail = '; '.join(determinants) if determinants else 'no determinant found'\\\\n        if antibiotic == 'ciprofloxacin' and not determinants and (gyr or quin):\\\\n            call = 'NA'\\\\n            detail = '; '.join(gyr + quin) + ' (reduced susceptibility; binary call uncertain)' \\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"rows.append([isolate, antibiotic, 'R' if determinants else 'S', detail])\\\", \\\"rows.append([isolate, antibiotic, call, detail])\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('output/methods.md');s=p.read_text().replace('The observed resistant isolates have the multiple-target pattern.', 'The observed resistant isolates have the multiple-target pattern. ISO_089 has GyrA S83L alone and is assigned NA for ciprofloxacin: this can cause reduced susceptibility but does not reliably resolve a binary S/R call without a breakpoint or MIC. Any lone acquired quinolone determinant without this target pattern would likewise be treated as unresolved.').replace('NA is reserved for an incomplete analysis or an unresolved mechanism that prevents a call.', 'NA is reserved for an incomplete analysis or an unresolved mechanism that prevents a call; all searches completed, so only the latter applies here.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_25", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_009"}
