{"cmd": "/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport csv\nout=Path('output')\nfor p in sorted((out/'amrfinder').glob('*.log')):\n text=p.read_text()\n assert 'amrfinder took ' in text and 'ERROR' not in text, p\n print(p.stem, text.splitlines()[-1])\nrows=list(csv.DictReader((out/'predictions.tsv').open(),delimiter='\\\\t'))\nexpected={(p.stem,a) for p in Path('data/genomes').glob('*.fasta') for a in Path('data/antibiotics.txt').read_text().splitlines()}\nassert {(r['isolate_id'],r['antibiotic']) for r in rows}==expected\nassert len(rows)==len(expected)==60\nwith (out/'methods.md').open('a') as f:\n f.write('\\\\n## Output validation\\\\n\\\\nAll ten AMRFinder searches completed successfully. \"'`make_predictions.py` reproduces the interpretation and checks 60 unique isolate–antibiotic pairs, the exact requested antibiotic labels, four columns, permitted prediction values and nonempty evidence. An independent final check compared the output pairs with the Cartesian product of input assemblies and antibiotic labels. The output contains 44 S, 15 R and one NA (ISO_089/ciprofloxacin). Raw primary reports, all-mutation reports and execution logs are retained in `output/amrfinder/`.'\"\\\\n')\nassert sum(r['prediction']=='S' for r in rows)==44\nassert sum(r['prediction']=='R' for r in rows)==15\nassert sum(r['prediction']=='NA' for r in rows)==1\nprint('Final schema and coverage checks passed.')\nPY\"", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "ISO_081 amrfinder took 41 seconds to complete\nISO_082 amrfinder took 28 seconds to complete\nISO_083 amrfinder took 46 seconds to complete\nISO_084 amrfinder took 32 seconds to complete\nISO_085 amrfinder took 43 seconds to complete\nISO_086 amrfinder took 34 seconds to complete\nISO_087 amrfinder took 30 seconds to complete\nISO_088 amrfinder took 34 seconds to complete\nISO_089 amrfinder took 50 seconds to complete\nISO_090 amrfinder took 37 seconds to complete\nFinal schema and coverage checks passed.\n", "stderr": "", "tool": "command_execution", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "item_27", "key_path": "item", "batch": "batch_009"}
